# MH <DOMAIN> Brain

A curated, interview-driven knowledge base for the **<DOMAIN> & Payments** domain at MyHeritage, paired with a Claude Code skill (`/<Skill-Name>`) that answers questions grounded only in the brain's content.

This is the pilot domain of a broader **MH Product Brain** initiative. The same pattern is intended to expand to Backoffice and Site domains.

## What's in the repo

```
mh-<domain-slug>-brain/
├── README.md                ← this file
├── SKILL.md                 ← canonical <Skill-Name> skill definition
├── brain/                   ← the knowledge artifact itself
│   ├── brain.md             ← curated narrative + facts per topic
│   ├── _meta.md             ← topic index (status, last-updated, refs)
│   ├── interview-log.md     ← raw transcripts (history of how brain.md was built)
│   └── references/          ← high-accuracy source docs (org chart, etc.)
├── docs/
│   ├── design-spec.md       ← the design spec the brain was built from
│   └── impl-plan.md         ← the implementation plan executed to build it
└── install.sh               ← deploy SKILL.md + brain/ to standard Claude Code paths
```

## How the skill works

`/<Skill-Name>` is a Claude Code skill with six commands. All answers are grounded in `brain/brain.md` and its linked references — the skill never fills in from general knowledge.

| Command | What it does |
|---|---|
| `/<Skill-Name> <question>` | Query the brain. Cites topics, sections, references, and tags status. |
| `/<Skill-Name> interview [topic]` | Run a structured interview on a topic and distill into `brain.md`. |
| `/<Skill-Name> verify <topic>` | Cross-check the brain's facts against linked reference docs. |
| `/<Skill-Name> status` | One-screen audit of brain health: coverage, stale topics, open questions, action suggestions. |
| `/<Skill-Name> capture <topic> "<note>"` | Quick in-the-moment append (dated history entry, fact change). |
| `/<Skill-Name> refresh <topic>` | Delta interview — what's changed since `last-updated`. |

See `SKILL.md` for full behavior and `docs/design-spec.md` for the architecture.

## Install (for new users)

```bash
git clone <this-repo-url> mh-<domain-slug>-brain
cd mh-<domain-slug>-brain
./install.sh
```

Then restart Claude Code so it picks up the new skill. Confirm with `/<Skill-Name> status`.

The install script deploys files to the standard Claude Code paths:

- `SKILL.md` → `~/.claude/skills/<Skill-Name>/SKILL.md`
- `brain/` contents → `~/Claude/brains/<domain-slug>/`

By default `install.sh` **copies** the files (safe — your clone can move or get deleted without breaking the install). Use `./install.sh --symlink` if you want changes to the deployed files to flow back into your clone automatically (useful if you're a maintainer).

## Adapting to other domains

This repo is a template for the <DOMAIN> domain. To build a Backoffice or Site brain on the same pattern, see `docs/design-spec.md` §9 (Generalization) and the README at `~/Claude/brains/README.md`.

